            <ArticleTitle>Proximal right coronary artery occlusion with ST elevation in all precordial leads.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>119.e1-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jelectrocard.2008.11.002</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present a case of a 55-year-old-man with acute coronary syndrome due to occlusion of the right coronary artery. Electrocardiogram showed ST-segment elevation in nine leads. We explain the causes of this exceptional electrocardiographic pattern.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
